//// `00 · 01-std` — refusing a duplicate `pub` DECLARATION was measured and
//// rejected (`libs/std` declares `parse` in `json`, `querystring` and `url`);
//// the refusal belongs to the consumer's unqualified USE. A bare
//// `import {parse};` over a project whose modules `a` and `b` both declare
//// `pub fn parse` brings in two different functions, and the use is refused
//// where it is written, naming both, on every target. commonJS and erlang
//// used to refuse the program with no line (`--> src/main.bp`), and wasm
//// linked one of the two and trapped. `import {parse} from "a"` says which.

pub mod a;
pub mod b;
import {parse};

pub fn main() {
    @print(parse("x"));
}
